assign_orphan_tags.user_template:
Analyze these orphaned tags and assign them to appropriate categories in the existing taxonomy.

TOP-LEVEL ENTITY SCHEMA (FIXED STRUCTURE - DO NOT MODIFY):
{top_level_json}

EXISTING TAXONOMY STRUCTURE:
{taxonomy_json}

ORPHANED TAGS TO CATEGORIZE:
{orphan_tags_json}

For each orphaned tag:
1. Determine the entity type (person, organisation, model, dataset, etc.)
2. Assign to the appropriate entity type parent (c_et_person, c_et_organisation, etc.)
3. Check if it's a synonym/variant of an existing concept
4. Provide confidence level

Return JSON with this structure:
{{
  "assignments": [
    {{
      "tag": "orphan_tag_name",
      "action": "assign|synonym|new_category",
      "entity_type": "person|organisation|model|dataset|etc",
      "parent": "c_et_<entity_type>",
      "synonym_of": "existing_tag_if_synonym",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "reasoning": "Why this assignment makes sense"
    }}
  ],
  "new_intermediate_categories": [
    {{
      "tag": "new_category_tag",
      "display_name": "Display Name",
      "entity_type": "category_entity_type",
      "parent": "c_et_<entity_type>",
      "description": "Category description",
      "for_tags": ["list_of_orphans_that_belong_here"]
    }}
  ],
  "unassignable": [
    {{
      "tag": "tag_name",
      "reason": "Why it doesn't fit anywhere"
    }}
  ],
  "summary": {{
    "total_processed": 0,
    "assigned": 0,
    "synonyms_created": 0,
    "new_categories": 0,
    "unassigned": 0
  }}
}}

Rules:
- PRESERVE the entity type structure from top_level.json
- Assign tags to entity type parents (c_et_person, c_et_model, etc.)
- Prefer synonyms over new concepts for variants (GPT-4, gpt-4 → synonym)
- Consider semantic similarity and domain context
- Entity types are FIXED - do not create new entity types

